-- title:
--   Second inequality in prime degree: norm-coset index divides p
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a Galois extension of $K$, let $p$ be a prime number, and assume $\dim_K L = p$. Let $B$ be an adelic base-change datum for the pair $(\mathcal{O}_K, K)$, $(\mathcal{O}_L, L)$, that is, a ring homomorphism $\beta \colon \mathbb{A}_K \to \mathbb{A}_L$ between the adele rings such that $\beta$ applied to the image of any $e \in K$ is the image of $e$ under $K \to L \to \mathbb{A}_L$, together with an isomorphism of $\mathbb{A}_K$-algebras $\mathbb{A}_K \otimes_K L \cong \mathbb{A}_L$ (the $\mathbb{A}_K$-algebra structure on $\mathbb{A}_L$ being the one given by $\beta$) carrying $1 \otimes f$ to the image of $f$ in $\mathbb{A}_L$ for every $f \in L$. Write $N \colon \mathbb{A}_L^\times \to \mathbb{A}_K^\times$ for the map induced on units by the algebra norm of $\mathbb{A}_L$ over $\mathbb{A}_K$ relative to $\beta$. The conclusion is that the index in $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ of the subgroup generated by the image of $K^\times$ and the image of $N$ divides $p$; in particular this index is finite.
--
--   This is the second inequality of global class field theory in the case of a Galois extension of prime degree, in its idelic norm-coset form: the group of ideles of $K$ is at most $p$ times larger than the subgroup of principal ideles times norms from $L$. It feeds the bound on the zeroth Tate cohomology of the idele class group in prime degree and the finiteness of the set of Hecke characters whose composition with the idelic norm is a given character.
